      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `eob \u003d\u003d 2 \u0026\u0026 tx_class \u003d\u003d TX_CLASS_2D \u0026\u0026 (unsigned int)(qcoeff[0] + NUM_BASE_LEVELS) \u003c\u003d 2 * NUM_BASE_LEVELS` (under `!CONFIG_ENTROPY_STATS`), `update_and_record_txb_context_output` (lines 638-643) and `record_txb_context_output` (lines 844-849) skip `memcpy` and only write `tcoeff[0]` and `tcoeff[scan[1]]`. Since `coeff_buf_pool-\u003etcoeff` is allocated via `aom_memalign` without zero-initialization, calling `av1_txb_init_levels(tcoeff, width, height, levels)` here reads uninitialized heap entries across the rest of the transform block (which triggers MSan/Valgrind errors in `av1_txb_init_levels_c` and skips the `eob \u003d\u003d 2` fast path during bitstream packing). Please add the matching `eob \u003d\u003d 2 \u0026\u0026 tx_class \u003d\u003d TX_CLASS_2D \u0026\u0026 (unsigned int)(tcoeff[0] + NUM_BASE_LEVELS) \u003c\u003d 2 * NUM_BASE_LEVELS` fast path here as well. (If GCC warned `-Wmaybe-uninitialized` on `levels` at line 410 because it cannot prove `scan[0] \u003d\u003d 0`, splitting `c \u003d\u003d 0` out of the `c \u003d eob - 2` loop to use `pos \u003d 0` / `tcoeff[0]` directly—like `warehouse_efficients_txb_loop` in `txb_rdopt.c`—avoids that warning.)",
